<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Reach Up is Vermont&#39;s monthly cash assistance for families with minor, dependent children, paired with case management to help you reach goals around work, education, housing, health, and more. Apply online, in person at your local district office, or by calling 1-800-479-6151 to request a paper application. You take part in an interview by phone or in person. If the child&#39;s other parent lives elsewhere, a child support case usually opens automatically unless you request a safety waiver."><title>Reach Up (Vermont TANF Cash Assistance) — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="guide-page"><div class="wrap guide-wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/programs/">Program Guides</a><span>›</span><b>Reach Up (Vermont TANF Cash Assistance)</b></div><article class="guide-main"><h1>Reach Up (Vermont TANF Cash Assistance)</h1><small>Last updated August 2026</small><p class="guide-lead">Reach Up is Vermont&#39;s monthly cash assistance for families with minor, dependent children, paired with case management to help you reach goals around work, education, housing, health, and more. Apply online, in person at your local district office, or by calling 1-800-479-6151 to request a paper application. You take part in an interview by phone or in person. If the child&#39;s other parent lives elsewhere, a child support case usually opens automatically unless you request a safety waiver.</p><a class="button primary" href="https://www.usa.gov/benefits" rel="noreferrer">Official site <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><div class="update-note">Program details can change—confirm with the program directly.</div><section><h2>Who qualifies</h2><ul><li>Eligibility depends on household circumstances, income, location, and current rules.</li><li>Applicants must meet the program administrator’s requirements.</li></ul><p class="maybe">You may qualify. The program makes the final decision.</p></section><section><h2>How to apply</h2><div class="apply-step"><b>1</b><p>Visit the official program website or contact the administering agency.</p></div><div class="apply-step"><b>2</b><p>Prepare proof of identity, residence, household size, and income.</p></div><div class="apply-step"><b>3</b><p>Complete the application and any required interview.</p></div><div class="apply-step"><b>4</b><p>Keep your confirmation number and copies of submitted documents.</p></div></section><section><h2>What to have ready</h2><ul><li>Photo identification</li><li>Proof of household income and address</li><li>Household-member and expense information</li></ul></section><section><h2>Common questions</h2><details><summary>How do I know if I qualify? <span>⌄</span></summary><p>The program administrator makes the final determination after reviewing your application.</p></details><details><summary>How long does an application take? <span>⌄</span></summary><p>Processing time varies by program, funding, and required documents.</p></details></section></article><aside><h3>Not sure this is the right program?</h3><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/help/vermont/">See all Vermont programs →</a></aside></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>